@startuml

start

:Thermal management controller executes as state machine on RTOS;
fork
  :Govern PWM fans;
fork again
  :Govern liquid-cooling loop;
fork again
  :Input signal validation;
  :Initialization;
end fork

:System verifies main processor's successful self-test;
:Check temperature and pressure sensor integrity;

:Spawn concurrent, prioritized tasks;
  fork
    :Periodic sensor data acquisition via protected ring buffer;
  fork again
    :Continuous system health monitoring;
  end fork

:Enter uplink phase;
fork
  :High-priority task packages telemetry with CRC;
  :Dispatch over CAN bus;
fork again
  :Lower-priority task monitors communication link status in real-time;
end fork

:Dedicated telemetry monitor;
fork
  :Implement bounded retries;
fork again
  :Exponential backoff for fault handling;
end fork

fork
  :Sensor fusion,calibration,and out-of-range checks execute periodically;
fork again
  :Critical faults engage redundancy;
  :Initiate controlled cool-down sequence via FADEC/BMS;
end fork

:Update operational state;
:Write structured audit logs to non-volatile memory within defined I/O budget;
:Update watchdog;
:Signal PMIC;
:Mmanage power states for standby modules;

stop

@enduml
